From: Valentin Haudiquet <valentin.haudiquet@canonical.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:38:52 +0200
Subject: fix(drm): include the SpacemiT K3 DisplayPort PHY module

The SpacemiT K3 (riscv64) display pipeline is built from three
modules: spacemit-drm (Saturn DPU), spacemit-inno-dp (Innosilicon
DP/eDP bridge) and phy-k3-inno-dp (Innosilicon DP TX PHY).

The module selection in 45drm finds spacemit-drm and spacemit-inno-dp
through the drm_crtc_init, drm_dev_register and drm_encoder_init
symbols they use. The PHY uses none of these symbols and lives under
drivers/phy/, outside the directories the generic catch-all scans.

The PHY is not a dependency of the bridge either. The only link
between the two is a devicetree phandle, which modprobe does not
follow.

70kernel-modules installs =drivers/phy on riscv64, but 45drm should
provide the KMS pipeline on its own. Add the PHY explicitly, guarded
by a riscv DRACUT_ARCH check, since SpacemiT SoCs are riscv64 only.

Signed-off-by: Valentin Haudiquet <valentin.haudiquet@canonical.com>
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/dracut-ng/dracut/commit/6842f083facfd8b31b9ef5fbd596213e0ebad0bf
---
 modules.d/45drm/module-setup.sh | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules.d/45drm/module-setup.sh b/modules.d/45drm/module-setup.sh
index 022d690..69143ae 100755
--- a/modules.d/45drm/module-setup.sh
+++ b/modules.d/45drm/module-setup.sh
@@ -19,6 +19,12 @@ installkernel() {
             "=drivers/video/backlight"
     fi
 
+    # SpacemiT K3: the DP PHY is only reachable from the bridge through a
+    # devicetree phandle, which none of the selection rules above follows
+    if [[ ${DRACUT_ARCH} == riscv* ]]; then
+        hostonly=$(optional_hostonly) instmods phy-k3-inno-dp
+    fi
+
     hostonly=$(optional_hostonly) instmods amdkfd hyperv_fb "=drivers/pwm"
 
     # if the hardware is present, include module even if it is not currently loaded,
